Compile upstream's downloader (core/libdivecomputer.cpp) without Qt, for threads.
It stays the code that parses dives and handles fingerprints. What changes:
- BLE_SUPPORT is on, and ble_packet_open comes from cpp/bindings/ble-stream.cpp.
- The QString address sniffing in get_supported_transports goes: BLE is the one
  wireless transport this build has.
- dive_cb, the fingerprint lookup and the fingerprint store take the core lock:
  they share divelog and fingerprints with ssrf::call() on the JS thread. See
  cpp/shim/include/ssrf-core-lock.h.
- import_thread_cancelled is atomic: another thread sets it.
- DC_EVENT_PROGRESS calls progress_callback, so the fraction reaches the UI
  rather than waiting for the next 10 kB message.

